Information Security Risk Register – Hopewell Medical Centre

1. Introduction

This risk register documents potential information security risks identified within the fictional Hopewell Medical Centre.

The purpose is to identify threats and vulnerabilities affecting critical information assets, evaluate their potential consequences and establish priorities for risk treatment.

The assessment uses a qualitative risk assessment methodology based on likelihood and impact.

2. Risk Assessment Methodology

2.1 Likelihood Scale

Rating| Description
1| Rare
2| Unlikely
3| Possible
4| Likely
5| Almost Certain

2.2 Impact Scale

Rating| Description
1| Insignificant
2| Minor
3| Moderate
4| Major
5| Severe

2.3 Risk Scoring

Risk Score = Likelihood × Impact

Score| Risk Rating
1–4| Low
5–9| Moderate
10–16| High
17–25| Critical

These scoring thresholds are project-specific assessment criteria.

